#passage(("I don't judge; the one who judges is God. He knows everything; he created you. Now Allah said when he created us he's given us something called the [fitrah]. It's an innate disposition that he created us with, first to recognize him as our Lord. So Allah, before he brought us in this life, he's given that within every human being to know that there is a Creator. You don't need to be taught that; it's innate within you. Now also that [fitrah] recognizes certain aspects of Truth and morality, like it's wrong to rape, kill, steal. They can be covered by society and then you can do these evil things, but innately you're born pure.", "Now what would guarantee is Allah says in the Quran he will show people signs within the Horizon and within themselves until it's clear to them that is the truth. The [fitrah] is going to be there when they're reading the truth from God; they'll have no option except to believe it. When I speak with Christian, Jews, anyone, and presenting to them why the religion could not be true, they have no answers: God cannot be a man; Jesus never said that he was God; he did not know, and God knows everything. You cannot escape clear truth.", "When you say to someone that Allah is unlike the creation, unlike anyone, unlike anything, created everything, has control over it, nothing happens in this universe except that he's aware of, this makes sense to the [fitrah] that is within you heart, so you wouldn't even argue with a statement like that. When you ask someone who even not familiar much with the idea of God, is God one or more, they essentially say is one, because they can recognize that through their [fitrah]. So what would guarantee that what I'm telling you now makes sense to you is the [fitrah] that you have.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Presents A Logical Problem With Hellfire In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WaGhbcZK2Cc", ((383, "6:23–7:02"), (436, "7:16–7:45"), (468, "7:48–8:18"),), id: 14)
