#passage(("For example, the Law of Non-contradiction: that's something which we believe is certain. We believe there cannot be a squared circle, because if it's a square, it's not a circle; if it's a circle, it's not a square. For example, this Law of Non-contradiction which I'm giving you, there are different things like it. So, we say, for example, the Intuitive Knowledge which is the idea behind the Law of Non-contradiction, or, for example, the cause and effect in relation to the Creation, because we know that we, as humans, we always look for a cause for anything innately. And these beliefs are true. We are saying the belief in a Creator is also innate.", "The highest form of knowledge is intuitive knowledge, universal intuitive knowledge. Why is it the highest form of knowledge? Because everything is built upon it. If it is not there, you cannot do anything. Everything has to be built upon intuitive universal knowledge, such as the fact that you exist. We have an intuitive universal knowledge that the Creator exists. We exist and the Creator exists, both of them. Therefore, Muslims accept this reality that there has to be a Creator out there, simple. What I mean by intuitive is that innate knowledge that is within you, that is not given to you by your outside factors. Your Society didn't give it to you; your community didn't give it to you.", "Is everything based on the idea that we exist, and that we can rationalise? And some of the laws of rationality is non-Contradiction that I was making to you, or cause-and-effect. Without knowing that I exist, without the Law of non-contradiction and without causality, can you do anything? No. That proves that everything is based on it. And if something is a foundation, is the foundation of knowledge and understanding, it is by definition higher than something which is relying on it, because it does not rely on anything else. It's independent, while other sources of knowledge have to rely on it. That's what makes this a stronger form of knowledge.", "To reason, to talk, to do anything, we have to rely on this Law of Non-contradiction, because if the Law of Non-contradiction is not true, then you cannot even use a language, because what I'm saying can mean the exact opposite of what I'm saying, which means you cannot even respond to what I'm saying. So, these things I'm telling you, without these things you cannot reason, you cannot live your life, you cannot do anything. And because they are universal, and we know they are true — because we can observe them being true — the idea of a belief in a Creator is also true, because it's one of those intuitive beliefs.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Conflicted Atheist Gets A Reality Check! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LxLsEe9Bu2k", ((468, "7:48–8:17"), (595, "9:55–11:14"), (706, "11:46–12:26"), (764, "12:44–13:23"),), id: 15)
// U ML310:276-306 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Islam says: can I have something from nothing? People are born innately knowing that there is a Creator, because Allah put that within us, so we don't have to play these games and excuses, there could be or there couldn't be. And I believe any basic human being looking at the universe, looking at the magnificence of the universe, innately deep down, no matter what he argues with his tongue, he knows deep down that there is a Creator that created all of us.", "And there are multiple people who came throughout time; most of them, what did they say? They said that there is a Creator. They agreed that there is one Creator, is One Entity that created us, and then they brought rules and regulations; they brought morality, telling us what is good and bad for us and what would happen to us after we die, what is going to happen in the next stage, what is going to happen in the afterlife. And through our investigation of those prophets and Messengers and reading the scripture, the Word of the Creator, the Revelation that comes from God, we come to conclusions, what is right and wrong.", "Even if I was not a Muslim, I can never argue against it. I know that I'll be a hypocrite to claim that there is no Creator, looking at the universe that way. I would say that I'm just arguing for the sake of arguing, as if it's sophistry happening. The reason I'm a Muslim is because I studied the evidence for Islam, knowing that Islam is the Truth. Message of Islam is very simple: there is that Creator that created you, and that you should connect to that Creator, learn about yourself, learn about the universe and practise the morality that is good for you in your life, because this life is a test whether you will do the right or the bad thing. And then there will be accountability in the Afterlife. Prophet Muhammadﷺ is one of those Messengers; we believe in other Messengers as well.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Unintentionally Proves The Accuracy Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tt_qknxI5I", ((906, "15:06–15:28"), (933, "15:33–15:51"), (956, "15:56–16:22"),), id: 16)
