#passage(("As human beings, innately anyways we are born knowing that there is a creator, not something that is introduced to you by your parents. There are studies on this.", "So they would ask children questions. There are similar studies on things like on cause and effect. It's also an innate thing. Like for instance you put a baby in a complete dark room and you touch it, and the baby looks, because there's no light; you don't see anything, but it looks because it assumes there's a cause for the touch. So there's ways to do these studies on the children. But similarly, there are methods of asking them about the creator. So you would ask them where does the world come from, or similar to that, anything to do with that; these children are able to communicate whether they believe in a higher power or not.", "So these are the studies, and all of the people are doing them are atheists. They're not Muslim religious scholars somewhere in Saudi Arabia or whatever. No, they're atheist scholars, and they're telling you human beings are inately born of that. And this is what Islam says. That Islamic teaching is being proved by atheistic social science.", "We can struggle with the idea: I want to live my life the way I want; I want to do whatever I want; wouldn't change the fact that there is a creator. So we can, like they say, beat around the bush all we want. But reality will always be reality. There has to be a creator. There has to be something who brought us into existence, just like you have to have parents and I have to have parents; I can't just exist without parents. And then Islam has it own proofs and evidences.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Apostate \"Philosopher\" Challenges Muslim On The Existence Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9hau-UgX-0Q", ((1261, "21:01–21:11"), (1362, "22:42–23:28"), (1408, "23:28–23:52"), (1436, "23:56–24:21"),), id: 18)
