#passage(("Where does the universe come from? Where do we come from? Where does everything come from? We just say to the people, can I have something from nothing? If you have 0 + 0 + 0, you always have a 0, even if you multiply that with infinity of zeros. We have an existence right now. The existence has a starting point. Some people refer to it as the Big Bang. But it cannot come from nothing.", "You have energy and matter compressed into a very small singularity. It requires a cause. There's something that needs to bring all of that into existence. And it is definitely beyond us humans, because there was no humans. There was no creation. There was no universe. And we say, whatever has the power, the ability to compress an entire universe into a small singularity and expand it, must be, by definition, what we refer to as God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Skeptical Atheist Rethinks Islam After A Rational Dialogue With A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T1bKr8UGkFw", ((6, "0:06–0:33"), (34, "0:34–0:59"),), id: 27)
