#passage(("This is not circular reason. I'll give you the reason why it's not. Let's take God out of the picture from the discussion. Can you have something from absolute nothingness? If there's creation today, there was no point ever that there was nothingness. It's impossible. So there was never absolute nothingness; that means there was always something. We know the universe has a starting point, so it's not the universe.", "There was matter, energy, that we know it's not conscious. So whatever the energy and matter that was in existence has to source from something else, and that is what started the whole universe. This is what we refer to as God. So when I say that God did this and that, I'm really just saying the entity, whatever the entity that have brought the energy and matter and caused the universe, is what we refer to as God. So nothing about this I believe a circular reasoning, because we agree that you canot have something from nothing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Presents Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NtXZBPaQ2NQ", ((483, "8:03–8:53"), (554, "9:14–9:46"),), id: 28)
