#passage(("Right now we're imagining because we exist. I'm saying if there was nothing, I don't exist, you don't exist. No imagination exists, no universe exists, no atoms, no planets, no stars, no space, no Dark Matter, nothing! \"Nothing\" is just a concept. For example, \"something\": the opposite of something is nothing. So it's something you can conceptualize, because all you have to do is use the opposite. That's why in dictionaries what they do sometimes is they define something by using the opposite. Like they say the definition of \"love\" is the opposite of \"hatred\". So you understand the concept of \"nothing\" because you know the concept of something.", "So I'm saying if there was ever nothing – which is the absence of something, there is no something ever – how can you ever have something? How can you have existence? There's no agency, there's nothing to create, there's no space for you to create in, there's no atoms for you to collect and gather. So everything has to come from \"something\". Where does space come from? So what is that something? is the question!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheists Challenge Muslim On The Existence of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZsW9t6W52Q", ((149, "2:29–3:25"), (209, "3:29–4:18"),), id: 29)
