#passage(("No scientist says you can have something from nothing. Because science says there's a law in science called causality. Every effect requires a cause. When you appeal to science, science is against you there, because they all agree that you don't have something from nothing. If you can have something from nothing, you don't need science. Why? Because then the rain comes, it's from nothing. I don't need to conduct science to realize that there is wind, and there is steam and all of that. Nobody believes something comes from nothing. That's why science operates, because they disagree with that.", "Actually, Big Bang is not an explosion. It's a very quick expansion. There is a slight difference there.", "Energy and matter is not conscious. It's like your shirt. It doesn't move and act on its own. This rock is not going to stand up one day and start walking. And that's not maybe, maybe not. Just like saying, \"Oh, maybe your shirt came from nothing.\" No, it has to come from something.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Atheist Challenges Muslim Then Gets Unexpected Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HQZVh00S7XM", ((407, "6:47–7:19"), (494, "8:14–8:28"), (566, "9:26–9:59"),), id: 47)
