#passage(("Energy is a physical thing, a part of the universe that is made and created. So energy does not make or create something. It's not a conscious being, not conscious entity. It's something that is physical within the universe, just like matter is, just like this rock is. So it cannot create or make. So if you believe in energy, the question still would remain is how did the energy come into existence? How did the full universe come into existence? That's a big question, and I'll give you the big answer.", "When you look at the universe, you can know the attributes of what made the universe using the universe. Meaning if I look at this table, I can know the attributes of the maker of the table based on the table itself. They require knowledge of language by necessity. They require to assemble material. They need a level of intelligence.", "Looking at the universe, you know that whatever brought the universe into existence requires knowledge that we cannot even comprehend, power, because you have these atoms: if you split, you have nuclear explosions, and the whole universe is atoms. It requires to be independent, meaning before the universe, to bring it into existence, it's not restricted by the things that we're restricted by within the universe, because he created all of them. He exists before us. So if you have all of these attributes, this is what people commonly refer to as God. This is by necessity, because the universe cannot exist unless there's an entity like that, just like this table cannot exist unless there's an intelligent person who knows language, etc.", "But this is something that we do not know as human beings. The reason is because we're in the universe. It's like imagine you have an ant inside a box or something like that. It's a hypothetical example. They do not know what's outside the box. You just live in the box. That's beyond what we can reach, and it's not relevant to us, because what's relevant to us is what happens surrounding us.