use, and whatever that cause is, is greater than any human conception. And that is logic!", "Now, to say science is going to know that in the future, that is \"the science of the gaps\"! That's not logic. That's not you being clever and saying: oh, people are just using God. No, people are not just using God, but people are saying rationally whatever that causes the universe will need to have: it's not limited by time and space the way we are, which means it's eternal, it sees the future, it causes the universe that is full of energy, it has power we can't even comprehend, it has knowledge that we can't even know about, because all of these gravitational systems and laws within the universe, and without all of these things I'm mentioning, you can't have a universe! So it's a fact that there has to be a creator. There's no gaps there.", "The gap is that you're trying to apply universe to bring some sort of a physical expression, because you're a Naturalist. You believe that everything happens through physical processes, but that cannot be proven, because you cannot prove science itself with physical processes. You have to rely on philosophy, mathematics, and other things, other abstract things. Science is limited. It doesn't know everything and it doesn't explain everything in the universe, and it never will! Pierce Morgan, for obviously his low skills and lack of expertise in this kind of argumentations about theology: for you to try to garner on that and pretend that he's doing \"god of the gaps\", when you are doing \"science of the gaps\"; it doesn't work here!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Does Islam Allow $ex Slavery? The God Of The Gaps Debunked| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UiCiBhmYPgQ", ((1598, "26:38–28:11"), (1697, "28:17–28:46"), (1731, "28:51–29:28"), (1778, "29:38–30:13"), (1817, "30:17–30:59"),), id: 72)

