#passage(("You can understand logically what the concept is: nothing is the absence of everything, to take everything out of existence and then have absolutely nothing. It's a concept that you can easily understand. Nothing is no thing. There's no thing that exists. That's what nothing is. That's the definition of it. There was never a point where there was no thing. That's the claim we make. God was always there. That's the point of eternality. But there was a point where we didn't exist.", "The idea of something and nothing and the idea of good and bad, these are two very different concepts, because the opposite of something is nothing. All you need to do is to subtract or remove the idea of something to have nothing. But it's not the same thing with good and bad. It's not if you just subtract good, therefore you would have evil. That's not a necessary conclusion. Good is an action of opposite of evil. You have to do something against good. So it's a fallacy to compare the two. You cannot equivocate the two.", "Also we can understand the concept of nothing. We have the idea of nothing on a mini scale in our existence. When you say there's nothing in my pocket, you can understand that this is something; if I take it out, therefore there's nothing in my pocket. So we already have the concept. All you need to do is to maximize a concept rather than minimizing it on something that you observe, you very fully clearly understand, on the concept of something or nothing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Abandons Logic And Rationality To Deny God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s5DUzwdtzqE", ((930, "15:30–17:23"), (1075, "17:55–18:57"), (1156, "19:16–19:42"),), id: 172)

