#passage(("A lot of people, in the Muslim community, do not understand the harm-effects of philosophy, the Western philosophy I'm talking about. Western philosophy instals within you something which we call \"doubt\". And that leads you to just contradictions. Because in reality, in order for us to live, we need to have certain things as assumptions. Like we have to assume we exist. The universe is in existence. The universe is consistent. Everything will continue to be the way it is. In order for science to work, we have to assume the sun will rise and it will set. So these are assumptions that you need. This basic kind of knowledge, if you don't have as a human being, you cannot function. Even in philosophy, there are assumptions. Like the Law of Non-contradiction, for example: two contradicting things cannot exist. All of these issues are assumptions.", "We say as human beings, Quran leads you to certainty. If you're certain you're existing, you're here, you also have to be certain that there is a Creator. Because if I'm here, I didn't create myself, I cannot come from nothing. There has to be something outside myself and the universe that brought us into existence. How do we know that this is God? By looking at the universe. So if the universe is like a lollipop, then I'm not going to say God made it, because anyone can make a lollipop. But the universe, because it's so complex, so vast, has so much design within it, you'd say that it has to be something with these characteristics.", "My advice for people is to stay away from philosophy. Do you know why people study it? They think they're intellectual and smart. When you're standing in front of the people, someone says, I study philosophy. Oh, that's amazing. I'm sure you are intellectual, but I'm saying you are intellectual without philosophy.", "The Quran, when you read it, a baby can understand it, and a farmer can understand it, and a professor can understand it. So Allahﷻ is sending guidance for everyone. Allahﷻ is not sending philosophical, very deep language that only you need a professor to understand. How can it be for everyone then? The philosophers themselves don't understand. They just speak without listening to it. And then when it comes around to it, they doubt their own selves. They put forward a theory, and then put forward a theory against their theory. So there is no sense in that. And they keep going in a circle, and nothing is ever certain.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Truth About Philosophy! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xoYG4Qi-lx4", ((301, "5:01–5:56"), (356, "5:56–6:30"), (390, "6:30–6:56"), (420, "7:00–7:46"),), id: 176)
