#passage(("Intuitive knowledge is that which you're born with. For example, you intuitively know that you exist. How can you prove that you exist? I'm talking proving to another person, not to yourself. You cannot prove the first personal subjective experience to a second, third person.", "Intuitive knowledge, I have a label for it: that which is universal and agreed upon. So intuitive knowledge that everyone has is not influenced by external factors like society or community. So if you were to put people in a village in Africa, they're not going to tell you LGBTQ values; they have to be westernized by the Western level of societies today.", "Another example: we're born as human beings innately knowing that there's a cause and effect. They conducted studies on children as well to see that. For example, you put objects on a table, then when they remove the table the objects didn't fall, the babies were shocked. So they're expecting a natural reaction to something. In a dark room you're expecting there's a cause and effect: there's an effect, there's a cause, something preceding. You touch a baby, the baby looks for who's touching it.", "Even some moral principles, I would say, we're born with it. Children: they give a cookie to one child, they don't give a cookie to the other child, and the child becomes angry. It feels a sense of injustice that have not been given an equal amount for whatever the other kid has been given. Some of these things are also innately born. And the idea of God: we're born innately believing in a high power, in a Creator, something above us. There are studies on that, for example Oxford University.", "So this, I would say, is the highest form. Why? Because everything is based on that. For me to start using reasoning, I have to first establish that I exist. No one has to accept this; I'm not saying Islam teaches you that, but I'm saying this is what I would label it as. But after it, of course, it'll be reasoning and deductive reasoning, etc.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Finds Logical Problems With Islam?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJuAdZhJIzo", ((429, "7:09–8:00"), (495, "8:15–8:56"), (538, "8:58–9:25"), (571, "9:31–9:55"), (600, "10:00–10:22"),), id: 181)
