#passage(("Why do you assume that the only type of evidence is scientific evidence? The word science means to know; it's about our knowledge. I was talking about the scientific method. Scientific method is to study the physical, natural world through experimentation, repeatability and falsification. So we only study things which we can empirically test. So there are other forms of logic and deductive reasoning that we use that can be a valid form of epistemology, which is a different source of knowledge that is not necessarily based on science. Like, for example, if I said to you, proof science using science, you're not going to be able to do that, because that would be self-defeating, circular reasoning. So not everything is proven through science.", "Science itself has assumptions. Like, for example, mathematics, reasoning, logic, things which are intuitive, like, for example, that we exist, that the universe exists; all of these are things which are assumptions that science has to rely on. Science relies on the idea that everything will remain constant: tomorrow will be like yesterday and yesterday will be like tomorrow and next week. All of these are assumptions that science cannot prove, that are not based on the scientific method, that are not testable, but without them, science cannot function. Mathematics, for example, is a form of deductive reasoning. Science cannot work without these things, but these things can work outside of science, and they are legitimate by themselves to prove the existence of specific things or not.", "Of course, science relies on testimony. Why do you assume all types of testimony are equal? All history is based on testimony, for example. But it's not a testimony of one individual who says X exists; it's multiple sources that are often separated by time or separated by space, that they would not be colluding to present that information, which makes that information reliable. If I'm going to my building and there is someone coming down and saying there's a fire, there's a fire, run away: that's one person, that's one testimony. Now another person comes, another person comes, another person comes, and all of them claiming that there is a fire. It's very legitimate for us to accept that testimony as a source of knowledge, unless we say all of these people are crazy, just running and saying there's fire for no reason.", "When did I say testimony is proof of God? Right now I'm not talking about God, I'm talking in abstract. I was talking about testimony being a valid source of knowledge. Now, to do with God or not to do with God, that's a separate discussion. All I'm establishing here is that there's something called epistemology, and these are different sources of knowledge coming to acquire knowledge about the world. It's not that the only way is the scientific method; no one believes that. Maybe some atheists do, but not the rest of the world, because the people who are practicing science themselves, they know that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Angry Atheist Challenges Muslim On Stream! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2l2wOowfqGg", ((366, "6:06–7:10"), (435, "7:15–7:55"), (533, "8:53–10:30"), (648, "10:48–12:17"),), id: 185)
// U ML096:491-554 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Criteria was: the scripture claims is from God, doesn't have internal, external contradictions. I say it's preserved, because if it's not, we'll have human writings and God writings, and we wouldn't know what to follow from what not to follow. Then the last thing: it has evidence of divine origin, which is the point I'm making right now. The evidence is as follows. Let's do this very quick experiment. Let's go back 1,400 years ago. Now, I want people to put themselves in that time, because 1,400 years ago there's no cameras, there's no microphones, there's no telephones, there's no airplanes, there's no cars, there's no microscopes, because we know the age where these things were invented.", "What do you mean you can't prove history? Do you disagree that phones were invented in a point in history? We have writings from people that existed that time. So we deny all history?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((1428, "23:48–24:33"), (1523, "25:23–26:16"),), id: 186)
