#passage(("Now you said it all comes down to whether that Scripture comes from God or not. But then you said \"that is a question that I'm not going to get an answer to in this lifetime\". I disagree. And I simply disagree because those people that you talked about that saw the miracles, they were not doubting whether the Prophet was a Prophet of God. Yes, they chose disbelief; they chose disbelief for other reasons. They chose disbelief for worldly desires, they chose disbelief for racist reasons, some of them: \"We're not going to accept the Prophet who's not a Jew! We're not going to accept this.\" They did not say that we don't believe that this is truly a Messenger coming from God.", "It's also the same with those who reject the existence of God, because when they see the universe, when they see the evidence, which everywhere around them anyways, they just need to look around, even within themselves, they know deep down there's a Creator (Fussilat41:53). That's why they say there's no atheist on a crashing plane! Because when it's coming down, they all scream \"Oh God!\" That's the only thing they're going to call to! So in reality, it's not about them \"not knowing\" it. So it's not the idea of what you said, knowing or not knowing, because we as Muslims, we believe in certainty. I believe that Islam is the Truth, 100%. I'm certain that Islam is the Truth.", "I would say it is impossible, and I'm going to make that claim for any human being. Bring me the smartest atheist on earth, whoever you want to bring me. They are unable to refute the fact that Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, rationally was a Messenger of God. It's impossible. Why? Because it wasn't just about what you talked about, like the miracle that the Prophet did in front of the people and the people saw. There are evidences that we can establish today, and look at today, and investigate today, that brings us certainty that he must have been sent by The Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((1692, "28:12–29:41"), (1788, "29:48–30:16"), (1836, "30:36–31:08"),), id: 190)
