#passage(("That is an incorrect way of looking at things, because that's a fallacy. Why? Because you're treating knowledge as if it is something that is being put under scientific method, like we have a theory and it's going to be falsified in the future or something. No! When I say, for instance, the Quran makes claims of prophecies, the prophecies have already happened! When I say the Quran, for instance, talks about things in the past, these things were already discovered to be true. So this is the argument: we've already established, rationally, that cannot come from Prophet Muhammad. If this information cannot come from a human being who existed 1,400 years ago, it has to come from God, as he claimed it does. It's not from him or his society, because nobody had this knowledge anyways. Then I've now accepted that this is divine Revelation. Done!", "Once I accepted this is the Revelation of God, now, if someone has anything to say, they need to bring proof opposite to it! Not only that, they also need to explain how did the Prophet do the things he did? There are no alternative explanations. So nobody can come up with them.", "There is something called reduction. When you reduce all options to one option, then that becomes an absolute fact. If I investigate: there is chocolate in the fridge, and it was eaten. There's only one person in the house, and the camera shows there's only one individual in the house, and he didn't leave the house. There's nobody else. Then that reduces to only one option, because nobody entered in and out, based on the cameras. Then that person must have been the person who ate the chocolate! When we reduce options, there's no alternative options, no alternative possibilities that exist. We remain with the last option as what we call an absolute objective fact. So that is now the statement I was making about certainty. When I say we are certain Islam is the Truth, that is the reason we're certain Islam is the Truth: because of the evidences that exist, nobody can refute it rationally. And no other religion possesses that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((2488, "41:28–42:15"), (2543, "42:23–42:59"), (2581, "43:01–43:57"),), id: 191)

