#passage(("The beginning of any field is to know at least the definition of what that field is, or what that thing is, in order for me to even start to embark on a journey of speaking about it. Now, to go to the extent of where you want to speak scientifically and tell us the scientific mistakes in the Quran, and how this is scientifically right, how this is scientifically wrong, when the foundation of what science is is not familiar to you, I think that is an issue, I would humbly say that.", "The definition of the scientific method is to study the physical world, the material world, that which you can put under a microscope. You do experimentation, then you do repeatability, and you do falsification. That is the definition of the scientific method. You have a specific experiment, you repeat that experiment, and then we see whether that experiment is falsified or is a valid theory for the time being, based on the limited data that we have and the research that we have. Now, something like this is by definition limited, meaning it does not bring you to absolute proof, absolute truth, absolute reality. All it leads you to is the best conclusion at the time, based on the data that we have.", "That's why you had, for example, Thomas Kuhn writing the very famous book called Paradigm Shift, where he talks about the huge changes in science, the things that people believed to be everything, and then it changes, like Newtonian physics, Einsteinian physics, the static state theory, and the Big Bang theory. These were things that people believed were absolute, or when you're learning in your book in the 1900s, you thought this was the universe, you thought this was reality, you thought this was the truth. But these major shifts and paradigms happened in science because science is an experimental thing that changes and adapts based on the new set of data, information that you possess as a human being. And it is limited due to the fact that you are limited as a human being. So it's a limited tool.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Claims The Quran Is Full Of Scientific Mistakes?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9P6vTJhCSlI", ((364, "6:04–6:26"), (388, "6:28–7:07"), (432, "7:12–7:50"),), id: 192)
