#passage(("A scientific method is the study of the physical world through experimentation, repeatability and falsification. Do you know who developed this method? It is a Muslim! His name is Al-Hassan Ibn Al-Haytham in Andalusia. His book Optics, who developed the new scientific method that you're using today. So when you talk to Muslims about science, we know very well what science is.", "So me drinking water is science? Right now we're doing science? Your definition, that everything is science; which scientist on earth define science to be everything? So on what basis are you defining science? There is an agreed upon definition: that science is the study of the physical world; we have to study things which are material. Is String Theory based on what's going on in the cosmos, which is matter? The universe is all atoms, physical.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “\"Really Smart\" Atheist Encounters A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NoDHTVV_RYs", ((460, "7:40–7:57"), (512, "8:32–10:08"),), id: 193)
// U ML384:115-150 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The people you listen to have convinced you. They told you: \"Look, you cannot be biased. You have to be an intellectual human being. You have to question everything.\" No, not really. You are born with certain things that are intuitive to you, that cannot be proved, that are axioms. For example, you cannot use science without relying on certain axioms. And if you really did not believe these axioms were true, you would not practise science. The only way you can practise science is to actually truly believe these things are true; otherwise, the method becomes useless, because what I'm basing the method on is itself not certain.", "So why would I practise a method which is based on uncertainty, that in the end would lead me to uncertainty? Are they certain? If the answer is no, then there is no point in me trying to apply my scientific method. It's just a waste of my time, because I know that these things are not certain. There are certain things every human being needs to accept and needs to apply to be certain about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Conflicted Atheist Gets A Reality Check! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LxLsEe9Bu2k", ((344, "5:44–6:24"), (384, "6:24–7:34"),), id: 194)
// U ML242:6-108 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Science is based on something called induction, and induction is: you look at the data and you come to the best conclusion based on the data. Now the data can change, and therefore the conclusion will change, which means that science does not lead you to objective facts. Gravity is not a scientific fact. There are scientific explanations of gravity: you have the Einstein model, etc. One of them is wrong, and now they moved into something else. So when there was a specific view of gravity in the past, it was taken as a fact; right now it's been changed. You have Einstein, and then you have the pulling force versus pushing force, etc. There isn't one model of gravity.", "Same thing when you say evolution. Which idea of evolution today is taken as an objective? Evolution, when you talk about mechanisms of evolution, you have many theories that adopt these mechanisms. When you mention mechanisms, you're not really mentioning all view. You want to talk about Darwinism? Darwinism have been moved; now there's something called Neo Darwinism. I'm not talking about whether it's good or bad. Good or bad is a different discussion. We're talking about does it lead us to objective truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Finds Logical Problems With Islam?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJuAdZhJIzo", ((41, "0:41–1:47"), (161, "2:41–3:35"),), id: 195)
// U ML097:199-262 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Religion and science are two separate topics in this case. One is inductive, that leads to temporary conclusions, and it's a useful method. And we say religion is reasoning and facts and logic that can give you absolute facts, true religion of course, not false religions. Science flourish under Islamic empire, because the scientific method they're using today, the modern scientific method, is developed by a Muslim, and his book Optics is how we have cameras. Algorithms is a translation of a Muslim name. Algebra, same thing, same story. So Muslims don't have a problem with science, but we use it as an instrument.", "Separating religion from prophet: I'm talking about a prophet, someone who comes, makes a claim: I am sent by God, God gives me revelation. That's what a prophet is. That's a claim. How do we identify whether this person is making a true claim or false claim?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises Sceptical Chemist With The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1ousrtPzAE", ((755, "12:35–13:20"), (811, "13:31–13:45"),), id: 196)
// U ML401:267-295 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("We say that it's impossible for you to ask for scientific proof for the Creator. I'll tell you why. Science is a tool. The first thing we say is that Allah is not physical like us. So how would I use a tool that studies the physical to learn about the metaphysical? So what we say as Muslims is that science has nothing to do with religion from the aspect of proving or disproving God.", "We say that we believe science is an instrument; it's a useful instrument to learn about the world, to get better technology. It's very useful; we learn it, we use it. But it cannot lead you to learn everything. For example, can science measure love, a person's love to another person? It's a metaphysical thing. \"Consciousness\": you got \"The hard problem of consciousness\". So, metaphysical, invisible. So we say that science can tell you how the physical functions, but it cannot tell you how the spiritual or the metaphysical or the invisible functions.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Native American Learns About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3MQgwBrdkhU", ((567, "9:27–9:55"), (597, "9:57–10:30"),), id: 197)
// U ML202:200-223 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("If the universe was created by a metaphysical being, then we cannot observe it being created using science, because science is a tool that studies the physical, and what created it was metaphysical. We already see that problem when you look at scientists and they're coming to the big bang and they say: \"At the point of big bang, all our laws that we apply today do not apply. There are infinite equations; we cannot calculate or understand what was going on at that time.\" It's beyond human tools, to put it that way. That's why they cannot tell you what was before the beginning. The question is always being asked. They cannot answer it, because it wasn't something physical; it wasn't something that is operating with the laws that we operate in, which is why you cannot tap into that reality.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Explain The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0EuiG8SUZM", ((651, "10:51–11:36"),), id: 198)
// U ML208:140-167 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("\"Science created us\": that does not make any sense. Science is not an entity that exists. Science is a concept, exists in abstract. If I say to you mathematics created us, is the same thing. If I said physics created us, the same. That's a concept that exists only in our mind. Mathematics exists in our mind, does not exist in reality. What is science? It's a method of studying something. How can a method of studying something, that is abstract, create anyone? Anyone who says that doesn't understand what they're saying.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hindu Questions Muslim On Polytheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Nbn5J51AtE", ((328, "5:28–6:21"),), id: 199)
