// U ML126:487-561 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("If you already admit that whatever you're going to present is things with no evidence or proof, it's not science then! Now you can call it philosophy, you can call it theorising about things, whatever term you want to use, but it doesn't fall under the definition of what is Scientific Method, which can be demonstrated, falsified or proven. So if it's not under the Scientific Method, you can use the term science all you want; just because a guy is called scientist said it, it does not make it science. Whoever is studying quantum physics and quantum mechanics today, number one, they call it baby science; number two, they tell you anyone who says they know anything about it, they don't know anything about it. So if it's just a bunch of theories that we're still discovering and learning about, it's not scientific knowledge.", "The things that you take the consensus or agreement of scientific community on right now, for example about cosmology, is not things which we are disagreeing with anyways! Whether it's the beginning of the universe, and all of these things, we agree: the universe, there's a beginning to it, there's a cause, and that cause will have necessary attributes. All we need to do as Muslims is to demonstrate the existence of what you refer to as an eternal Entity that creates the universe through whatever you want to use, naturalistic process or whatever process you want to say, but an eternal entity that is powerful in a way you cannot comprehend, and knowledgeable, and brings the universe. You can say you're Atheist all you want, but once you make that definition, you're stuck now: that this entity, by definition, will require will. And also you cannot say that it's restricted by natural laws when it is literally the one that started the natural laws in the universe that we are living and existing in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Philosopher Challenges Muslim On The Creation Of The Universe! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?