#passage(("If you ask me about Islam, I respond first with our evidences and then I critique Christianity. I'm not going to get offended; that's not disrespectful. Disrespect will be abusive words, cursing and this. But if I was to say something and I not factually correct, then it could be offensive.", "Your argument is called an argument from ignorance. Number one, you claim there's an argument for preservation of the Biblical scripture; you've not provided what the argument is. And then I've provided you from your own tradition what your earliest manuscripts are, what [your] scholar say and what is the names of the book. My argument is based on evidences. I give you names, manuscripts, books, etc. I give you references. And then you argue from ignorance. You saying, I'm sure there is flaws, I don't know what they are, but I'm sure there's flaws in your tradition, and I'm sure there's arguments for our tradition, I don't know what they are, but I am sure they're there. It's called an argument from ignorance until you present them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christians Challenge Muslim On Evidences For Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M8FdFU3haa8", ((1494, "24:54–25:27"), (1552, "25:52–26:32"),), id: 222)
