#passage(("Do we exist in this life so we can live forever, or did God give every single one of us a time where we will leave this life? I'm younger than my parents, but I could die before my parents crossing the road, and I could get hit by a car. Nobody is here to live forever. Only one who's ever living is God. The method of how we die can be different from one person to another. Plus, I'll tell you something which a lot of people don't consider as well. Sometimes we exist in this life, there's a lot of distractions around us, and sometimes difficulties can come in our life to remind us of why we're here as well.", "But there's something that is very important to understand: that we don't just exist in this life. There's an afterlife. I could lose my family members, but they're not gone forever. So, it's only if I live an atheistic world view, then do I believe that we turn into dust and that this is the final separation between me and them. Not only is it cruel, but it makes no sense, because I didn't create myself. Your parents did not create you, because if they give you life, they're not going to cry when you die. Because they didn't give you life to begin with. They just gave you that vessel, the body, and God has given you that soul, the consciousness that you and me possess.", "So Allah has created us and he put us in this life as a test. When does your test end? When you take the paper. That paper is your life. Whenever it's taken, only God knows when it's taken. So Allah has given a chance for your parents, and he's given me a chance, and he's given a chance for everyone for this lifetime that they live. Even if I die today or tomorrow, I believe I've had my chance to research Islam, to look for the truth, and to pass that test by doing the best I can in this life. So true success is succeeding the test by dying upon the correct understanding and doing as much good as you can in this life. You exist here for a reason.", "Someone comes and tells me there'