#passage(("We don't believe we have original sin. So, why do you think we live in a world? We exist in this life according to Islam to be tested. Meaning whether you choose to do good or evil, you have choices every day. You can see a poor person, would you feed them or not? You can see your neighbor suffering, would you help them or you will not help them? So the suffering you see that you think of it to be evil has wisdoms that can be good relative to other people. For example, I can see someone without money and I can appreciate God's giving me money. I can thank God for giving me money. Can be an opportunity of God to test me whether I'm going to help them or not going to help them in their time of need.", "And if we are being tested, that necessitates difficulties. Why does paradise exist? Pleasure. So, why do you expect to have pleasure here in this life? Never ending pleasure. That's essentially what your question is assuming. If we don't have suffering, that would mean that we only have pleasure. You're missing a very important aspect, which is the afterlife. This life doesn't end.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Ladies Discover The True Identity Of Jesus! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ytiIPe7Dmho", ((942, "15:42–16:20"), (982, "16:22–17:16"),), id: 313)
