#passage(("This is something in philosophy they talk about, they call the problem of evil. We would say, even if there was evil in the world, how does evil alone disprove the existence of a higher power? It might debunk in a way a higher power that is All-Merciful or this or that. But it does not deny the existence of a higher power.", "So now let me answer from our perspective, what we believe as Muslims. We say that Allahﷻ created us in this life for a reason. This life is then a test, whether you will choose to do good or you will choose to do evil. Now, in order for me to punish you, should I give you the choice to do good and evil or no? In order for me to test you, should I give you two choices? If I give you one choice, is that a test? So I have to give you two choices.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran (TaHa20:134) (if We were to punish those who did evil, before them doing the evil, then they would say \"we haven't done anything wrong\"). \"If you only sent us the Messenger, we would do good\". So, Allahﷻ is saying you have to allow them to also take the actions of doing good and evil in order for Allahﷻ to test them. So even you can do good, I can do good, but there will be people who will do evil. There will be people who will fail the test and there will be people who succeeded in the test. So there has to be evil in the world.", "We're born with certain privileges, me and you. We're born with a house. We're born with family. We're born with food, food in the fridge. We take these things for advantage, because we had them from the beginning. If you always had good from the beginning, you will take it for advantage. But when Allahﷻ tests you and He gives you a little bit of difficulty, you appreciate the good things that He's given you as well. So, Allahﷻ is saying in the Quran that (He tests you with good and evil to see whether you will be thankful or not) (Alanbiya21:35).", "So, Allahﷻ tests us in this life so that we can go back to Him. If my life was always perfect, I'm never going to go to Allahﷻ and say, thank you for giving me this and that, or call upon Him, help me when I'm in a bad situation. People remember God when they're in difficult situations. So Allahﷻ sometimes makes that situation for you to remember. Sometimes Allahﷻ makes a difficulty in your life to raise your level in Paradise, to remove the sins that you did. We might do evil. So Allahﷻ gives us something hard in this life to take away the sins that we did. The wife of the Prophet, she said (even the pinch that you have, small pinch, it moves from your sins). So Allahﷻ moves away the punishment. He doesn't punish you. He gives you these things in life in order for you not to be punished in the Afterlife.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Truth About Philosophy! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xoYG4Qi-lx4", ((916, "15:16–16:00"), (962, "16:02–16:30"), (993, "16:33–17:16"), (1062, "17:42–18:09"), (1096, "18:16–18:56"),), id: 315)
