#passage(("Atheists, they try to pretend \"I'm going to do it as a Socrates Method\" and then he's just making an emotional argument. Either you want to do things rationally, or if you want to lay on an emotional level, you can go to some Christians; maybe they would like emotions. But here I deal with facts and reality. Because it's a test for me; I'm not God. God is the One Who creates the test.", "The equivalent of what you're saying is a teacher giving a test to the students. Why is the teacher not giving the answers to the students when they are in the test? Because he's the teacher, he's not a student! The students are the ones who are dealing with the test; the teacher is observing the students. So your question of why does God not save the child: because God is the one who is putting us in the test, we are in the test. So God does not interfere with our test. He is not stopping us from doing something, because otherwise it's not a test.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Philosopher Attempts To Challenge A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hGbkF45B_A0", ((524, "8:44–9:42"), (590, "9:50–10:10"),), id: 331)
// U ML305:82-132 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Someone saw a child drowning and is able to save him. He does not save him; that's immoral, yes! If God go and start to prevent all immoral actions from taking place, there will only be moral actions, in which therefore there will be no choice between moral and immoral, which means this life cannot be a test. In order for a test to be there, there has to be 2 choices between right and wrong and between good and bad, which would mean that good and bad has to actualise in reality.", "You're just viewing the death of the child only regarding the child, but I'm telling you that the child is a pixel in a big picture. So that picture would be his family, would be people surrounding him. The death of a child is a test for the parents, the death of a child is a test for the family. So there's a lot of variables that you're not taking into account that is considered a test in this life.", "And anyways the children that die Islamically, they go to Paradise. If a child dies and goes to Paradise, that's a reward for the child, not a punishment. If I'll go to paradise if I die as a child, I would say OK, dying as a child is better than living this life and maybe being on the verge of maybe entering Paradise or not. So you're just coming to the problem of evil, which is a very basic argument that's been dismantled so many times.", "God is the source of objective morality. So He determines what is right and wrong for us to do. He is the standard of right and wrong; whatever God does — because God is good — whatever He does is morally good. You're conflating us with God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Philosopher Attempts To Challenge A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hGbkF45B_A0", ((223, "3:43–4:24"), (281, "4:41–4:55"), (300, "5:00–5:19"), (347, "5:47–6:01"),), id: 332)
// U ML169:281-335 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("If the Creator intervenes, then how are they tested? Whenever I'm suffering I ask God, and God just do it; all the suffering I have, ask God remove it, God removes it the next minute. The prophet told us the more righteous a person is, the more the test, the difficult the test you get. Why? Because if you are a stronger believer, that means you can endure a stronger test. What makes people great throughout history is the suffering that they've been through and they overcame due to their strong faith. That's why we say these were the best of Believers. We say the prophets, for example, were the best people because they had more suffering than anyone else.", "Prophet lost all of his children except his daughter Fatima, the only one that was left, with Hassan, Hussein, and she died straight after him as well, like 6 month after him or so. So the prophet lived a very difficult life. His first, most beloved wife, she died, Khadijah. And then he had this life of suffering in Mecca for 13 years, people attempting to [kill him]; he had to flee, to go away. His own family members, uncles, trying to kill him, turning against him. He's told that his father is in the Hellfire; his mother, Allah told him not to go to grave and seek forgiveness for. If you look at the life of the Prophet, you will understand that the more righteous you are, the more difficult the test you go through, and overcoming them is what makes you an example for other people, essentially.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Chinese Revert Shares His Conversion Story To Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7yAJVFrfEBk", ((754, "12:34–13:39"), (821, "13:41–14:26"),), id: 333)
// U ML320:613-660 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("We say that Allahﷻ does the things the way it befits His Majesty, the way that He knows, because He's the Most-Wise. If he decided to give a specific type of evidence to a specific type of people, a specific type of way — because every Messenger had a different type of Miracles, by the way; so not all of them brought the same thing, all of them brought different things — so Allahﷻ, based on His Wisdom, to those specific people, He will give certain things. So today Allah has not given us that, because Prophet Muhammadﷺ is the last and final Messenger, and the one that performs that Miracle is the Messenger, and there's no Messengers today coming. But Allahﷻ says in the Quran: (That we will show them our signs within the Horizon and within themselves until it's clear to them that it is the Truth) (Quran41:53).", "The difference is you are punished in this life and you're punished in the Afterlife. Either way, the person will be punished. So if the Miracle is done in a way which is undoubtable, observable, in front of your own eyes, then the hastening of the punishment can happen sometimes by Allahﷻ based on His Will. Now, researching and coming to the Truth, Allahﷻ chooses to punish you in the Afterlife. But still, even Allah can punish people in this life, but not necessarily those type of punishments of the people of the past where a whole Nation is completely destroyed. But he punishes you throughout your life by getting depression, losing your money; all of these type of different punishments, it can apply to yourself. So everything is based on Allah's Will there, because Allah's Will operates in accordance to Allah's Wisdom, and He will show the signs to the people based on His Will and Wisdom.", "Everyone is getting a different test even today, because it depends where you're born, it depends what your physical capacities are; because someone is born in a completely different state than you are. Someone is born today in a country in which it has been bombed. Allahﷻ, based on His Wisdom, He gives the test, because Allahﷻ says in the (Quran2:286) (That we do not overburden a soul except what it can handle). Allah will give you a test that you can handle depending on your situation.", "So we say that Allahﷻ does what He Wills (Quran21:23) لَا يُسْأَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْأَلُونَ (He is not asked about what He does); we are the ones who are asked, because we are the Creation. So, in essence, you're asking me why does the All-Wise — you, the limited knowledge, unwise person — why does the All-Wise choose to do things in a specific way? I don't think I can give you an answer for that.", "But Allahﷻ sent different Prophets and Messengers. Prophet Muhammedﷺ, Allah determined to preserve his Message, so there is no need to send other Messengers; because the Message is preserved — the Quran — is here today and will always be preserved until the Day of Judgement. The question is, other than worrying about other people, shouldn't you be worrying about yourself? Where are you gonna end up?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Irrational Criteria For God's Existence! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xz7nptUD9Ug", ((2478, "41:18–41:53"), (2517, "41:57–42:39"), (2607, "43:27–43:47"), (2636, "43:56–44:12"), (2652, "44:12–44:30"),), id: 334)
