#passage(("You're assuming everyone is going to suffer in his life; that's not the case. You only suffer when you choose to suffer. How do you go to Hellfire? Hellfire is a choice. Who said the test is really hard? It's hard to look at the universe and recognise there's a Creator? No, that's easy. So step by step. The first step, we already agree it's completely easy, because even you don't need to look at the universe. We know that children are born believing in a Creator. Studies have mentioned multiple times stuff like this, like the Justin Barrett study in Oxford University, etc. So we're already born believing in Allah. Allah said in the Quran that He has already put that (Ar-Rum 30:30). So there's nothing hard about believing in a Creator, because you're born innately with that belief.", "Second thing, establishing Islam is the Truth. I've already given you evidences now that I've not come across a single person who's been able to refute it, or will never be anyone who's able to refute it. So there's nothing hard to come to the conclusion that Islam is the Truth if you've actually done some research and spent your time asking the correct people.", "Now on top of all of that, I would say that Allahﷻ is The Most Merciful with His creation, and it's the biggest act of ingratitude to claim that it's difficult, when Allahﷻ says in the Quran: (When you do a good deed He gives you 10 times the reward, and when you do a bad deed it's just one bad deed) (Alan'am 6:160). If you have an intention to do a bad deed but you don't do it and you stop, Allah gives you a good deed. You were going to do something wrong but you didn't do it, so Allah gives you Hasana حسنة (a good reward).", "Allah says that when you give Sadaqa صدقة (Charity) or when you give Zakat زكاة (Almsgiving) or charity or any of these things, that He multiplies it until 700 or even more if He wills (Al-Baqarah 2:261). This is when you do good things. And anything that He prohibited you from doing, He's given you a better alternative. You do not have intercourse before marriage; He's allowed you to marry. Don't drink alcohol; drink juice, drink milk, drink honey, drink anything else. This is not good for you, so don't drink it. It is an act of Mercy from Him to tell you not to do these things, because they're harmful for you.", "When you read the Quran, each letter is 10 Hasanat. And Allah says in the Quran: إِنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ (If you do good deeds, they will remove the bad deeds) (Hud 11:114), without you doing anything. So the minor sins that you do, just doing good deeds is enough for those minor sins to go away. All of the bad deeds that you do, how do you get rid of them? You just repent. You sincerely regret the action, then you repent to Allah and He will forgive it.", "What is hard about this? There is nothing easier than to follow what Allahﷻ have told you to do. That's why the Prophet said: \"إنَّ الدِّينَ يُسْرٌ\" (Verily, The Religion is easy). Allah is not asking you to fast every Monday and Thursday or to pray 24 hours. He's only given you five prayers, and each prayer takes two to three minutes; 15 minutes of your day you're gonna pray.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Afghan Girl Claims That Muslims Are Blind Followers?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7HhWSHopwFc", ((1952, "32:32–33:13"), (1998, "33:18–33:28"), (2016, "33:36–33:57"), (2043, "34:03–34:27"), (2077, "34:37–35:01"), (2101, "35:01–35:19"),), id: 335)
