#passage(("Allahﷻ, when He says (alBaqara2:30) \"I know what you do not know\", He also gives us examples in the Quran. For instance, He gave us this Quranic example in Chapter:18 of the Quran (alKahf), where Allah gives the example of someone called alKhidr and Moses. Allah is teaching us from this story that we can perceive something to be evil; that doesn't necessarily mean it's evil.", "So, in that story you have Moses and alKhidr. There are three incidents that happened; I'll just give you one. They were looking to go to a specific place and there were some people in a ship. They give them a free ride. They're very nice, very accepting. He said: \"Come, we're going to take you for free, we're not going to take any money from you.\" So, they took them with them. Then alKhidr, who was with Moses, started making a hole in the ship. Then Moses said to him: \"How could you do this!? These people took us for free. How could you return their favor, essentially, by damaging their ship?\" So, alKhidr said to Moses: \"Didn't I tell you you're not going to be able to be patient with me?\" He told him in the beginning: \"You're not going to be able to be patient with me.\" There are three things he did, and every time Moses said: \"How could you do this!?\"", "Now, in the end, when alKhidr explains to Moses, he says: \"Now, this is separation between me and you. I told you you're not going to be able to be patient with me. Now, let me explain to you.\" He goes on to explain to him the situation of the ship. Why did he do that on the ship? He says: We were passing in the sea and there was a king. We're going to go by a king; that king takes every perfect ship. That king, if he sees a ship and that ship is good, it's perfect, there's no issues with it, he takes it for himself. So, he made that specific damage in the ship; this is a favor for these people, because now that king is not going to take their ship when they cross by the king.", "When you see the situation, you assume: \"Oh, this is terrible, this is horrible, how could you do this!?\" But this is the first vision, because you don't have the full picture, the full image, the full wisdom behind what happens, and who has all wisdom is The Creator. You might perceive something you don't necessarily understand; you think it's evil, you think it's bad, you think it's suffering, but in reality, that is good for you. You might suffer: you have a very bad toothache, but that toothache is actually giving you a warning: \"Go to the doctor, there is a big issue happening here.\" It's actually helping you, so it's good. Pain and suffering are not bad in every situation. If you're not familiar with medicine, you go to the doctor and you see them amputating someone's arm, and you say: \"How could you do something so horrible!\" But there's a disease that would spread to the rest of his body and he's going to die. You don't know the whole picture, you don't know the whole wisdom. So, you perceive something, in the first instant it looks like it's horrible, but it's not.", "Allah tells us in the Quran (alBaqarah2:216): كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌۭ لَّكُمْ (Fighting has been prescribed upon you, and you hate it, you dislike it) وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكْرَهُوا۟ شَيْـًٔا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ (you may hate something and is good for you) وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تُحِبُّوا۟ شَيْـًٔا وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَّكُمْ (you may love something and is bad for you) وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ (Allah knows and you do not know). This is the important thing: God has the full picture, has the Ultimate Wisdom and Knowledge. That's why these things that we perceive are not necessarily bad for us. There are many wisdoms we can see in life.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Asks Muslim To Explain Why God Allows Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5-bfwhR0lSM", ((285, "4:45–5:01"), (304, "5:04–5:47"), (351, "5:51–6:27"), (387, "6:27–7:14"), (439, "7:19–7:47"),), id: 337)
