#passage(("One important thing is looking at the life of the Prophetﷺ. Prophetﷺ from our perspective, he is the best of Human beings, he's the one that we're supposed to follow, to imitate, to look at his life. But looking at his life, what happened to him: he had 3 male children, all of them died young, age of two and younger than two; he had daughters, all of them died except one; he had granddaughters and they all died as well, in his life! Everything in his life: his wife died in his life, his uncle died and mutilated in his life. So if you look at his life and you look at the test that he had, you mentioned being poisoned by that woman. All of these tests that happened in his life; it is because of his level of righteousness. Allahﷻ says in the (Quran29:2-3) أَحَسِبَ ٱلنَّاسُ أَن یُتۡرَكُوۤا۟ أَن یَقُولُوۤا۟ ءَامَنَّا وَهُمۡ لَا یُفۡتَنُونَ ۝ وَلَقَدۡ فَتَنَّا ٱلَّذِینَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ فَلَیَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِینَ صَدَقُوا۟ وَلَیَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱلۡكَـٰذِبِینَ So Allah will make it evident, will make it clear the true believers from those who are not true believers.", "So Allahﷻ tests everyone. He tests you. You were on the verge of accepting; you are sure that this is the Truth, \"OK I'm going to take that step\" can be a test for you. And also Satan has an influence; there is no doubt he will have an influence by putting ideas in your mind, or even putting ideas in that friend of yours that you would not expect him to talk to you, but Satan whispering in his mind making him talking to you, trying to stop you from doing that. We will say I believe in Allahﷻ. And Allahﷻ, if I rely on Him eventually, it would be good for me, even if I get a disease and die. Why? Is that necessarily a bad thing? If you believe in Allah,ﷻ you accepted Islam and you died, where are you going to go? You would go to Paradise. You've just accepted Islam, so all the previous sins are forgiven. So you would be very lucky in that situation, so disease is not necessarily a bad thing.", "Also Allahﷻ says (Quran42:30) وَمَا أَصَابَكُم مِّن مُّصِيبَةٍ The problems that happen to you in your life, فَبِمَا كَسَبَتْ أَيْدِيكُمْ It's because of what you've done! There's a lot of bad things that happen to us in our life that we deserve to get because of the evil that we did to other people, things that we've done in the past, Etc. So there's many explanations I can give you for this idea. Everything is a test, and it happening in that time for you is a test for you. But still, Allah's given you the chance here, you're still alive today.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Romanian Asks Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eixflyogKg4", ((1106, "18:26–19:26"), (1171, "19:31–20:57"), (1261, "21:01–21:36"),), id: 343)
