#passage(("You claim that a person who suffers is who has done nothing wrong. Who did nothing wrong in this life? Is being born doing something wrong? What happens to them in the afterlife? That would only be unjust and evil and bad if that person who's born and died is going to go to Hellfire, for example, or going to suffer.", "At the same time, you said \"Oh, I don't believe that God is this\" or \"God is that\" or that \"This life is a test\". Well, you either take the worldview that God exists and then your question makes sense, or your question makes zero sense, because if there is no God you cannot blame God for anything! So, it's either you premise your question, which is based on an assumption that God exists, or you say, \"I don't believe in God\" and then we discuss a completely different topic, whether God exists or not. But to come when there's already a worldview that exists that there is a Creator, and then that Creator told you that this life is a test, \"I don't accept that\" — that makes no sense, because we already operate under that premise. If we don't operate under that premise, then we start from the beginning, whether God exists or not, and we have a completely different discussion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Atheist Receives A Reality Check From A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ha146KFce5w", ((561, "9:21–9:53"), (610, "10:10–10:54"),), id: 345)
// U ML230:190-213 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("We talk about the baby. In this life that we exist, this baby does not live in an abstract world; the baby lives in a world where there are other human beings. So first is that these babies do not have suffering in this life that we would have if they were continue to live their life.", "Number two, then now the other aspects of the pictures that many people don't see, which is a test for the people around the baby, test for the person who caused the killing or do evil, for the family members who lose the baby. So there's many elements. That's why we say cannot take things as abstract concepts out of reality. There are many other things that are around it. There is answers, and there's clear answers and logical answers and good answers and would satisfy the person in Islam. I would guarantee you that, because I talk to Christians, I talk to every religion, I've been talking to people from different religions for a long time. So the fact is Islam will satisfy this rational, if you're open enough to listen and investigate and read; that's the only thing that the Islam asks you, or God asks you to do. You can always ask God for guidance; you don't need to ask me or ask any human being. If you try, you'll see it will work wonders. But the answers are there for the questions that you ask.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Presents Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NtXZBPaQ2NQ", ((934, "15:34–15:58"), (985, "16:25–17:20"),), id: 346)
