#passage(("If this life is a test, then by definition there will be difficulties and there will be suffering. Allah in the Quran promises us as believers (alBaqara2:155) that we will have suffering, we'll have loss of life, loss of wealth, we'll have diseases, we'll have difficulties in our life. And as Muslims, we are completely understanding of why we go through difficulties, because if there are no difficulties, there's no test! Now we talk about children dying, for example. We, from our Islamic point of view, believe when children die, they go to paradise. So, if anything, that is a reward for them, rather than being a punishment; that is actually a bounty of God that God has bestowed upon them. Whichever amount of suffering that they go through in this life, which is very minimal, it's not equal to the eternal, never ending life of happiness.", "We have a tradition in Islam where the Prophet tells us that \"the man who suffered the most on earth in this life\" — now, you can imagine \"suffer the most\" means what in this life: probably lost all his children, lost all of his.. just go with your imagination as wild as it gets — and the Prophet tells us: \"when that person is dipped into paradise, then taken out, Allah will ask him, \"Have you ever seen any difficulty?\" And then he will say, \"Oh, by You God, I've not seen any difficulty\". Why would he say that? Because the bounties and the rewards that he will see is going to make him forget everything! And we're talking about the person who suffered the most in this life. So if these children go to paradise, then in this reality this is a bounty and a blessing that God bestows upon them. The fact that this life is a test responds to everything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Atheist Receives A Reality Check From A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ha146KFce5w", ((264, "4:24–5:03"), (309, "5:09–6:09"),), id: 347)
