#passage(("A test is one of the answers. It's not a [cop-out] to say it's a test, because without suffering you [cannot] have a test anyways. Life being a test is one of the main things, but there are so many other things. Your suffering can be a test for your relative. Would you take care of a person who's suffering who is a family member of yours? That's a test for you, not just a test for that family member. Also can be a way for you to appreciate what you have. Everyone is the same level, the same thing, we cannot recognize differences between one another. If I see another person who is in a lesser status than me — that's why the prophet said look at those who are beneath you or under you, do not look at those who are above you, because then you'll appreciate the blessings Allah have upon you. You have two hands; there's someone who has no two hands and arms. You're able to breathe and function; there are people who need these machines just for breathing because they have a problem in their body. So you'll appreciate the blessings that you have.", "And also it's an opportunity for you as an individual to help others. There's someone else who's suffering, who's in need; I do not suffer, I'm not in need, I have access to, let's say, money, wealth, whatever. That is a test for me: am I going to help that person who's in need, who suffering, or am I going to look at them and laugh? Are you going to despair in the mercy of God, are you going to be a True Believer and stick to your faith? Allah says we will surely test you: loss of money, loss of wealth, hunger, and even restraining yourself, that is a form of suffering. Then Islam will be a problem if there's no suffering; Islamic concept makes no sense, because you cannot test anyone in this life of anything; everyone is living happily, nicely, nobody's suffering.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Chinese Revert Shares His Conversion Story To Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7yAJVFrfEBk", ((521, "8:41–10:35"), (635, "10:35–12:07"),), id: 350)
