#passage(("Animals, on the Day of Judgment they will be turned into dust. They're not going to go into Paradise or Hellfire or anything like that. But animals can be a test for us: us perceiving their suffering, us causing them suffering. For instance, our actions causing animals suffering can be a reason for us to enter Hellfire actually. There's a narration the Prophetﷺ told us: there was a cat, a woman locked that cat, did not feed it, did not give it a drink, until it died; that woman entered Hellfire for doing that action. The Prophet also told us another story about a woman that was, let's say, a prostitute; she was doing evil deeds in her life, and she was walking, then she saw a dog. The dog was thirsty, his tongue was out; she went into the well and used her shoes, and gave that dog water, and Allah forgave her for that reason! So, these animals' existence is also a test for us of how you will deal with them, how we will treat them, etc.", "There's a story about a prophet: he was bitten by an ant, he destroyed the whole colony. Then Allah spoke to the prophet and He told him: Why not only the ant that hurt you? Why did he destroy their whole life and existence? Because these animals in this life, they exist for our sustenance, they exist as a test for us, they exist for multiple reasons, and they exist to glorify Allah. Allah says in the Quran (alisra17:44) (There's nothing except glorifies Allah in their own way, but we don't understand their glorification); we don't understand their languages.", "But even between animals, because Allah is the Most Just: the animal that hit the other animal; one had two horns and another had no horns. The Prophet told us on the day of judgment Allah will seek retribution for that animal to hit the other animal. Because it didn't have horns in this life, on the day of judgment it will take back its right and it will hit it back like it was hitting it. Even between animals, Allah is teaching us this. Justice will even extend to this Animal Kingdom.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Asks Muslim To Explain Why God Allows Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5-bfwhR0lSM", ((569, "9:29–10:21"), (624, "10:24–10:52"), (655, "10:55–11:21"),), id: 352)
