d in the same way. Anyone who wants to kill, wants to rape, wants to do anything, God can just take away the ability from them and stop them. Then why would he test them to begin with?! If Allah allows us to choose, there will always be people who are choosing evil and doing evil. And there are more people not choosing it. Are there more people who are choosing evil, or more people who aren't choosing it?", "You're referring to the situation in Gaza. So, don't you think now that when you say that you want God to do something, that he's already doing something? In fact, I'll tell you something interesting. Throughout the last 70, 80 years, this has been going on. People only knew about this after October the 8th. Now, people are saying: Oh look! That's a horrible thing happening. Of course, 100%. No one who has any sense of humanity will disagree with that. So, for those people who see this cruelty that happens, isn't this a way for God to show them as well who's good and who's bad? Isn't this a way for God to show people, other people with a strong faith, that no matter what happens to them, they will stay connected to God, follow God's guidance, and they will believe in God because they know this life is not everything? OK, a missile falls or whatever, I'm dead now. It took only 2 seconds. Then, they'll have an Eternal Life in Paradise. And that person who did this to me, when he dies as a disbeliever, Eternal Hellfire is waiting for him.", "The minute we understand the dynamic of life: that this life is a test, and what is going to happen is not going to remain eternally, and injustice is never going to succeed in the end, it's never going to be victorious, Allahﷻ told us that. In the end, the believers will be the ones victorious. Can it take time? Of course, it will take time. This is not a new thing, but because of it, there're so many wisdoms, and there are so many good things that Allahﷻ has allowed to happen through this.", "People are learning about what's 