#passage(("We need to read everything in context, and through reading things in context, then you can understand things. So I cannot take the end of a story and then ask why the end of the story is happening the way it's happening without the whole story. Imagine watching a movie or a series, going to the last two minutes, where someone's dying, and saying: Oh, I don't understand why this person is dying! OK, why haven't you watched the two hours, or I don't know how many hours, depending on if it's a series, of the whole story taking place?", "Now, when you talk about, for example, the flood of Noah, or people dying, as an example, you say, why? Allah gives us a story in the Quran. Allah answers your question in the Quran. Noah spent 950 years calling his people to the Truth (al'Ankabut29:14). And Allah in the Quran has given them signs. Each Prophet of God comes to the people with signs. Like today, we don't have a living Prophet, but when there is a living Prophet, Allah gives them signs. Allah tells us in the Quran, He sent these Messengers and He gave them signs (alHadid57:25). So that Messenger came and he showed the people signs of why he is a Messenger of God. We talk about signs and things that humans cannot do. For example, you heard the story of Moses splitting the sea, turning his staff into a snake, all of these things, things that humans cannot do, to demonstrate that he is sent by that Creator.", "So the people of Noah, 950 years being called. And he's being mocked continuously; nothing, there was no chance. So then Noah made the supplication to God (alMuminun23:26) that these people, there's no hope for them. And he asked Allah to bring a good generation, a generation that there is hope for, that they will accept the Message, and not to leave any of these disbelieving people (Nuh71:26). He made that supplication; he said لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ (do not leave on earth any of this generation). If you leave them, they'll just continue corruption (Nuh71:27), and they'll only be disbelieving people. So, these people were punished after this! After this period, after the signs are showing to them.", "Allah tells us in the Quran that when a sign is given to people — we're talking about a Major Sign, a sign that nobody can deny, a sign that, if you see, you know for a fact this is a Messenger from God — Allah tells us in the Quran that once these signs are given, then there's no more warnings. That's it (alAnaam6:158): you believe or you're punished, if a sign like this has been given to you. So many of these Nations, many of these people have had these signs happen to them, and they still rejected, they still disbelieved, they still continued in their transgression, and they were worthy of being punished, and God punished them for that.", "So it's nothing there about, like you call it, interfering or not. No, they had plenty of chances, whether it is the time period that I mentioned, whether it is the evidences that were demonstrated to them without any shadow of a doubt, that leads them to: no doubt this is from God. And they don't deserve any more time, because once you've had a sign that cannot be denied, then time for what? Time is for people who are doubtful, time is for people who are not sure. That's why they're given time.", "Imagine I'm a Messenger of God sent to you, in a hypothetical situation, and you say, OK, show me that you are a Messenger of God, and I just do like this and the moon disappears or something. I tell you, this is a sign from God, it's not my power, or something similar; of course, I'm giving you an example. And I do multiple signs to you, and there's no way this is just a human being, if he's doing this. And it's not just you seeing it, but other people are seeing it too. Then you choose to continue to disbelieve, or the whole nation continue to disbelieve. Then there's no more time that should be provided for you.", "Your example was voided of context. I just provided you the context from the Quran. Allah says in the Quran (alIsra17:59), for example: وَمَا مَنَعَنَاۤ أَن نُّرۡسِلَ بِٱلۡـَٔایَـٰتِ إِلَّاۤ أَن كَذَّبَ بِهَا ٱلۡأَوَّلُونَۚ Allah is saying, as response to some people who are asking for signs, that they're not getting any more of these Major Signs, because earlier people disbelieved in them. And then Allah mentions an example: وَءَاتَیۡنَا ثَمُودَ ٱلنَّاقَةَ مُبۡصِرَةࣰ The people of Thamud, which was the Nation, Allah has given them this animal, which is a sign, which was a huge animal, etc. Some sign that came out of a mountain, etc. But something that they knew was from God. They disbelieved in it. And then Allah says: وَمَا نُرۡسِلُ بِٱلۡـَٔایَـٰتِ إِلَّا تَخۡوِیفࣰا (These signs that we're sending, Major Signs, they're only warnings). So they were warnings to the people: you believe or be punished. That was what the Messenger said to them. The people choose to be punished. So, what can you blame God for anymore?", "The minute you say everyone will die — yes, if everyone will die, then why does it matter if God takes their life in this way or that way? You said \"die naturally\". This is an atheistic term. What do you mean by naturally? There is no such thing as nature. Nature doesn't have an effect on people. Nature is a Creation of God. That is a set of laws that God has placed. Life is only taken and given by God. If God gives you life, and decides to take it after giving you every chance out there to take, why is there a problem? God can take your life whenever He wants. He gave it to you to begin with. So when you talk about \"He gave us free will, He take it away\": He didn't take it away! He has given you the choice in this life and the test. And once you, after every chance that has been given to you, deny, then yes! You deserve to be punished. Assuming that person lived for 10 more years, that doesn't change anything. If the person, once they fully had the evidence presented to them, still rejects, then what does 20 years change?", "The people who have their \"longer time\" or whatever are those people who haven't been presented with proofs, ultimate proofs and evidences, like these ones that you can observe with your own eyes of these Messengers doing. You haven't had this proof given to you. Yes! God has given you time. He's allowing you now! You're speaking to me! You used some disrespectful terms at the beginning of the discussion; God didn't take your soul! He's not like: you know what? It's time for you to die, because you said something bad. No! And it's not only you, actually. There are people who are cursing God day and night. There are people who go burn religious scriptures, insult God and Messengers of God. God allows them to live, because this life is a test. We haven't had this opportunity, or this proof, which is undeniable. So they are still in the period of their test. If God wanted us to be believers, he would make us believers (Yunus10:99).", "Even the term \"kill\", I would say, is a term that is used by humans, used with each other. We just say God takes your life. He's given you something. He's taken it back. Imagine I give you a bottle, then I took it back. It's my position in the end. It's MY thing. We say something in Islam. We say (AlBaqara2:156) إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّآ إِلَيْهِ رَٰجِعُونَ (we belong to Allah, and to Allah we shall return), because we, as whole Creation, have been made by God. God created us. We belong to God in the end. The soul that we have has been given to us by God.", "So this term kill, which can be dramatic in a way, it doesn't apply to God in that way. When we do it with each other, we do it for emotional reasons, for enmity, hatred, all of this stuff. God doesn't need any of that, because He's The One Who gave it to you. And if he wanted to punish you from the start, if he was like some atheists are trying to portray Him, He wouldn't even allow humans to exist! He just puts you in Hellfire: you've got to do bad, you go to Hellfire! Because He knows. So He still gives you the chance. That blessing that God has given to you, it's His right to take it away when He wants.", "Who's given that human life? You're complaining about God! So it's either you say God exists or doesn't. How can you blame God if God doesn't exist? This is the game that atheists play. You want to blame God, but at the same time you tell us God doesn't exist! So if you want to blame God, God has to be in the picture. And if you want to blame God that exists, then you have to also accept that narrative that God is The One Who gave that life, because you're blaming Him. Or He doesn't exist; now you're blaming Him for anything! This shows inconsistency on your end. It seems you have other emotional reasons, or could be whatever other reasons, issues that you may have with God, but those don't change these realities I gave you. And in the worldview where God exists, in every faith, He's The One Who has given them the life. So when you say human life is valued, who gave the human life to begin with anyways?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Refutes Inconsistent Atheist Criticizing The Actions Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eOMW7R6z_wg", ((118, "1:58–2:25"), (149, "2:29–3:15"), (202, "3:22–4:04"), (252, "4:12–4:48"), (291, "4:51–5:24"), (329, "5:29–5:56"), (380, "6:20–7:18"), (508, "8:28–9:32"), (582, "9:42–10:37"), (668, "11:08–11:41"), (705, "11:45–12:35"), (775, "12:55–13:51"),), id: 357)
