#passage(("To just claim that people choose where to go or where not to go, then where did they originate from? You're saying souls are being generated, but you haven't told us how are they being generated. What is generating them? Where are they coming from?", "Do you believe that you cannot kill human beings under any circumstance? And then you said: yes. Then I said: OK, if that is your belief, which you've asserted, then if someone is coming to slaughter your whole family, and everyone in your entire building, we shouldn't stop them? This guy has weapons and he's going to shoot people back, and the only way to stop them is what they would refer to as \"deadly force\". So, you're allowed to take human life just depending on the context. So why is it so bad when God takes human life in His own Just context and Wisdom? When it's in your human context, it's OK. But when God does it, it's not OK! Because you value human life so much, you said.", "When you are a disobedient person, are you putting other people in danger? When you are a disbeliever of God, a corruptor in the land, a killer of Prophets, like they were doing, are you doing danger to other people? You mentioned Sodom and Gomorrah, for example. If you were reading that story, you would have read with your own eyes, when God sent angels, and then they saw them, they threatened to kill Lot. He doesn't allow them to do indecency with those people. So if those people are threatening to kill other people, then why cannot God take the life of those people who want to threaten and kill other people? Under the same context, which is preventing people from taking the life of other people, or causing injustice in the land or corruption or whatever, why is that not good?", "So if you are in danger, not me, and someone is trying to do that to you, and I'm a police officer, I shouldn't stop them, because it's not me? As a police officer, I'm allowed to stop the person who's causing you harm. So it's not about happening to me anymore. So it's not about happening to God or not. If God is taking the life of someone who's causing harm to others, under the same logic that you use with the police officer now, why is that OK for the police officer, but not OK for God?", "Of course God is involved in the efforts of human beings, just like the police officer is involved in the efforts of people. You're saying: He does it here, but He doesn't do it there. It doesn't change the fact that when he does it, it's completely fine. Hopefully you'll actually rethink your positions, and actually come to logical, rational situations, not emotional, like \"I read this book, and it gave me comfort, therefore, what the book says is true\". That's not how rationality works; things work with evidence, not how it makes you feel. There's many people who read many things, and engage in many things, and it gives them comfort. It doesn't, therefore, mean what they believe is, therefore, true.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Refutes Inconsistent Atheist Criticizing The Actions Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eOMW7R6z_wg", ((1503, "25:03–25:15"), (1530, "25:30–26:46"), (1634, "27:14–28:24"), (1732, "28:52–29:23"), (1815, "30:15–31:38"),), id: 358)

