#passage(("You can never find out whether you have free will or not if you believe in a Creator, or if you accept the idea of the existence of a Creator. When I say Creator I mean you believe in an All Powerful, All-Knowledgeable Entity. So you cannot reconcile between an All Powerful, All Knowledgeable Entity that Wills everything in existence, that Knows everything in existence, that Created you, and at the same time the fact that you have — no, I wouldn't use the term \"free will\"; I don't like to use that term anyways, because we don't believe we have free will. You've got Free Will and you've got hard Determinism, and you've got people who are completely Libertarian, the concept of free will, and you've got a school in the middle called Compatibilism, which tries to reconcile between the two, and there's various arguments that people make for that. But in an Islamic perspective, we say this is not something that the human mind can explain rationally. I cannot explain to you rationally, using examples, that the Creator is All Powerful, All-Knowing, Wills everything in the universe, and He's given me the choice to choose that which deals with my Afterlife at the same time.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clever Atheist Pushes Back Against Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dToXMJpuY70", ((280, "4:40–6:03"),), id: 361)
