#passage(("Even Atheists have to grapple with this concept, whether you're religious or not. So, you'll get people like Sam Harris who will try to claim that everything is Determined, while you'll have other people who say: No, you have free will. Because even if they don't believe in God, they still believe in causality, and if there is causality, then things are determined materialistically, if you don't believe in the Unseen. So, it's not really a criticism towards Islam or a criticism towards any specific religion. I would claim: if you don't believe in God, and you're a materialist, you're forced to believe that everything is determined. You have no choice. If you claim that everything is not determined, you're just pretending. If it's just Materialism, then everything is a consequence of another thing. It's a Cause, \"Causality\". Where you are today is a cause of where you were before. But Muslims believe we're not just materialistic beings; it's a Soul. And this is where the idea of choice comes in as well. It's not just physical beings, and cause and effect is what determines everything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Questions Muslim On Free Will In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6uEKa9ZO9u4", ((346, "5:46–6:48"),), id: 368)
