#passage(("If this life was a test, and that test is whether you will believe in God and follow His commands and whether you would reject Him, would it make sense for God to give you a sign that He exists while He's testing you whether you believe in Him or not?", "I don't believe you. I know you live your life knowing that you have a free will to choose what you do, what you're choosing. So if I kill you right now, you don't believe that I should be blamed for that? I'm trying to say that if I do that, I should not be held accountable, because it was something forced, I didn't have a choice in.", "Actually the Quran has a very interesting verse about that. The Quran says what you're saying, and it says that people who don't believe use that as an excuse not to believe. So it says that: سَيَقُولُ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا لَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مَا أَشْرَكْنَا (Quran6:148) Those who disbelieve, they say if Allah willed, we would not have disbelieved. So Allah says this is how they disbelieved and this is how their ancestors disbelieved, using that excuse.", "And I know that deep down you know that you're living — when you do your day-to-day things, you do them based on you making your choices, but when it comes to believing in God, all of a sudden this idea of free will comes into the direction. Which to me is a bit inconsistent; it is like the same people who come to me and say I do not know if this existence is real or this and that. This is the same hypocrisy. I say: OK, why don't you go in front of the bus? And jump off the top of the building? Why don't you live your life based on the claims that you make that this life might not be real? No! You live your life that this life is real, but when I talk to you about God's existence: Oh! Maybe not everything exists, maybe this.. When it comes to God, all of a sudden, there is a complete different kind of argumentation when it comes to God. Completely different criteria. Why? Because deep within, the person does not want to believe in a Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clever Atheist Pushes Back Against Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dToXMJpuY70", ((51, "0:51–1:01"), (76, "1:16–2:12"), (176, "2:56–3:18"), (206, "3:26–4:06"),), id: 369)
