#passage(("Guidance and misguidance is going to be an outcome of the decisions that you make. Allah, in the Quran, says that He doesn't guide the wrongdoing people, for example, the فَـٰسِقِينَ, those people who choose to do evil, people who choose misguidance. Allah says (alJathiya45:23) أَفَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَـٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ (Have you seen the one who took his own desires as his god?) وَأَضَلَّهُ ٱللَّهُ (Then Allah misguided him). So what does Allah misguiding him mean? It means that he did choose to make his god his own desires. That is the misguidance that he's in.", "It is not that Allah misguides someone who's sincere, looking for the Truth! Guidance is also an outcome for the actions that you make. Allah says in the Quran that (alAnkabut29:69) وَالَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا فِينَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا (Those who struggle to find Us, We’ll guide them Our ways). So, if you struggle, and you try to find guidance, and you try your best, Allah will guide you! If you choose disbelief and disobedience, Allah will misguide you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Apostate Reveals Her True Colours After Getting Exposed! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NTgbl-R9v_0", ((225, "3:45–4:33"), (296, "4:56–5:20"),), id: 375)
