#passage(("We don't say humans are nothing; that's one extreme. And we don't say humans can fulfil whatever, \"create their reality\"; that's another extreme. The One that creates reality is The Creator, The One that created the world, created me, created you, and The One who has given you abilities, has given you power, gives you provision, takes away from me, gives you life and takes it from you, is The Creator. Now, you cannot create your own reality, but you can take the means to acquire something. So that is the middle ground that Muslims are in.", "Allah in the Quran, for instance, He says (He's The One Who provides) (adDhariyyat51:58). But in the same time, He tells you to go and walk in the earth and work and make money (alJumu'a62:10). He doesn't tell you to sit down and wait for money to come to you. So there's a combination there. The way Allah will provide you is through the means that you take, and the more means you take – working, being intelligent, trying to do different things – through these means, Allah will increase you in the provision that He gives to you. So you don't get the money because of the means; you get it because of God. But with the means is a reason for you to achieve that in the end. Because someone can do the means and, in the end, not achieve what they want, because God did not give them that thing. So you cannot create your own reality.", "I'll tell you a very funny thing. I remember when I was younger, way younger, I watched this guy on TV. He was someone who's a gambler. You know these stickers that they bring, and they scratch to see who's the winner of whatever it is. He was doing these things, and they brought him because he's been for 25 years scratching stickers and he never won a single time. He spent all his money for 25 years trying to \"create his reality\" by winning. \"I'm a winner.\" Imagine, 25 years he's spending money. He's become homeless. I wouldn't have that patience, I'm not going to lie to you. I'm not going to scratch these stickers for 25 years!", "So you can take the means, you can do everything. You have many people who are failures throughout human history who did \"believe in a reality\" to the extent that they spent all their money on a project. They did everything! But the project still didn't work. Because you don't create your reality and you don't give success to yourself. The One who gives you success is God. So, you can take the means, and God can give you success and provision, or you can become a failure even though you took the means, because you don't create your reality.", "Sometimes what we want is not that which is good for us. As Allah says in the Quran (alBaqara2:216) that (you may want something or love something, and it's bad for you) (and you may hate something and it's good for you) (And Allah knows and you do not know). And that's why, if you were creating your reality, you would probably create your destruction most of the time, than you would create your happiness, because humans are driven by their own selfish desires.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tyson Hockley Grills The Muslim Lantern With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XGBP8LOEhg8", ((428, "7:08–7:35"), (457, "7:37–8:18"), (500, "8:20–9:08"), (554, "9:14–9:38"), (590, "9:50–10:07"),), id: 380)
