#passage(("I've read the Bible. I've read the Shiva writings there that I was reading. That's your scripture. It's not my scripture. But I read it and I see inconsistencies and problems. And that is why I know more that Islam is the truth. Because the more I'm reading in your scripture, the more I'm realizing why it's not true, cuz it's confusing. It doesn't give you clear guidance on what is morally right and what is morally wrong. Like you said, you have to meditate and figure this out on your own. But I'm a subjective being and I can come to conclusion different than yours and then there's no right or wrong. That's why I said there are many of these Hindus that follow these stories I were mentioning and do these things and this is their conclusion. That's a problem that causes chaos.", "You need guidance as human beings. When you go to the law in this country, they don't give you subjective law and say go interpret it the way you like. No, they tell you, if you cross the red lights, you have this [fine]. If you kill this person, you have this punishment. If you [steal] this, you have this punishment. Rules are clear on the act because human beings require guidance from God. Don't think you just go do whatever you want to do. No, there has to be right or wrong and has to be clear parameters of right or wrong. And that is what Islam is about. It's about guiding people to the truth. I know they're too many to read. Whereas Islam is only one, simple guidance from God because it's from the creator. There's only one creator. There's no being with the creator. There's one creator only created everything and knows everything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hindu Debates Muslim On The Rationality Of Hinduism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_kyQX24QTmQ", ((1093, "18:13–18:51"), (1131, "18:51–19:58"),), id: 408)
