#passage(("We believe as Muslims [we're in] this life to be tested, tested meaning that whether you will choose to do what is good, and that comes from God. So the test is whether we'll do the good or we'll choose our own desires and what we feel like and Satan.", "You heard about Jesus, Moses, Noah, Abraham. All of them claimed to be prophets and Messengers from God, and they did not say different things about God. If you were to look at the teachings of Jesus, Jesus did not say what Christians believe, which is the Trinity, father, Son and the Holy Spirit. He didn't teach that. There's nothing like this in the Bible. He [taught] there is one Creator worthy of worship and you should submit to him, which is what Islam teaches. Moses [taught] there's one creator. Even Christians would admit that he didn't teach the Trinity. Abraham taught the same, David taught the same, Solomon taught the same. They all taught that you're here in this life and there are certain commands that you need to obey and follow, which is the commands of God, because he created you for a purpose.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Philosophers Challenge The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=agqDQQkQf2A", ((423, "7:03–7:22"), (456, "7:36–8:11"),), id: 414)
