#passage(("I say there's only one god. So you cannot compare because there's only one God anyways. But the question is do we have the right understanding of that God or are we making things up about God. The only way I can know about you for sure, where you from, what your name is, you going to tell me. I can make assumptions. I can be right. I can be wrong. That's why I'm saying making assumptions is not the right thing to do. That's why God tells us about himself. There's only one creator of the universe. That creator, what is his attributes? Every one you ask, they will agree. They will tell you who's all powerful, all knowing, created the world, Merciful, is not bound by time and space, the way we are, knows the future, all of these things.", "But what we should care about is why did he create us? Why did he put us in this life? And he has sent us multiple prophets and messengers. I believe in Jesus. I believe in Moses. I believe in Abraham. I believe in Noah. I believe in Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon all of these messengers. I believe in all of them. They all came with one message that there is that creator, and the important is not the human being, the important is not the messenger. The important is the creator who created you, that he gives you this message from him which gives you the moral basis.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist And Muslim Debate The Consequences Of Following Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3f7FdlJFatQ", ((435, "7:15–8:02"), (482, "8:02–8:30"),), id: 417)
