#passage(("Definitely, there is peace that the Quran is bringing and all of these things. But this is not the main purpose of sending the Quran. Quran is a Book that is sent as a Guidance. We as human beings, we need guidance, we need laws, we need to be told what is morally right, what is morally wrong. We need these rules in our life. Structure, and also answers for the questions that are essential to your existence, like \"Where did I come from?\" \"What's going to happen to me when I die?\", \"Who's God?\", \"Is there Heaven and Hell?\", \"Is there an Afterlife?\"", "These are all questions that you cannot discover on your own; you need an external entity to tell you. You need the Creator that created you and created the world to tell you. That all has to come through Revelation. So the Quran's job is to do that, is to give you the Guidance and to tell you what you need to do, how to submit to your Creator and Maker, and a part of that submission is the peace that you mentioned, that you will have peace in the world through submitting to your Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Should We Doubt Everything?! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xcAO_agqBFE", ((97, "1:37–2:06"), (131, "2:11–2:32"),), id: 419)
