#passage(("How would God communicate to humans without using language? Even the Holy Spirit, according to the Christian narrative, gave words to John and Matthew and Mark and Luke. We Believe Islam is the full truth. Revelation is God fitting in something: I think that's a misunderstanding. God can reveal the [full] truth related to you in a scripture; there's no problem.", "[Khidr], which was, we believe, also many scholars believe, is a prophet who was with Moses, and a bird came and he took a drop of the sea, and he said to Moses that my knowledge and your knowledge is like that drop in the ocean in comparison to the knowledge of God. So essentially we're not saying this is all knowledge; we're saying this is all truth related to us, related to human beings and the functions. We only hold a drip of the drop of the knowledge.", "We don't need full knowledge; we're not God. I do not need to know things outside my realm. For example, I need to know that which is guidance for me. The Quran is guidance for mankind, the truth related to what they need to know, how to behave, how to function, what they need to do, moral aspects of life and all of these things, and the identity of God, not based on assumptions that we make. So when you open the Quran you'll see it will describe God using words, because it's the words of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Philosophers Challenge The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=agqDQQkQf2A", ((1401, "23:21–24:31"), (1473, "24:33–24:59"), (1504, "25:04–25:32"),), id: 420)

