#passage(("Now we have the prophets and messengers of God. If the creator created us, he's not going to just leave us lost like this in this world. It's not like you give birth to someone, you run away, I'm not going to take care of that. He's going to also guide us to the truth. He's going to send us people to bring us closer to him. He's going to send us people to tell us this is wrong and this is right. Because even though you may have some knowledge of right or wrong that is given to us, we don't have complete knowledge of right or wrong.", "And the proof of it is us today, different countries, different laws. One country, different states; America is like 100 countries in one country. Every state has its own laws. Here you can carry a gun; you cross to the different state in the same country, you cannot carry a gun. You'll be put in prison. So, we as human beings, we are unable to agree on anything. Even the most basic and fundamental things. We need something that brings us together that is objective.", "Why do we say God's objective? Is all-knowing. He's all-wise. So, if God commands us something and he says this is right or this is wrong, he made us. If I made this, I would know everything about it. I would know every detail of what's good, where to put it, what temperature to use, whatever. We say the creator is the one who created us; nobody would know what is good and bad for us more than the creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((459, "7:39–8:07"), (488, "8:08–8:34"), (514, "8:34–8:53"),), id: 421)
