#passage(("God sent you prophets, he sent you Messengers. How many people said we are from God? Many people. You had Jesus, you had Moses, you had Noah, you had Abraham, you had Prophet Muhammad. All of them came with the same message. They said there's only one God, but God controls everything, created everything, gives life and takes life away from people.", "And then they bring you Revelation. Why do you need Revelation? For two reasons. First, to tell you your purpose in life. Why do you exist? Why did God create you? He made you, so this will tell you why he made you. But it also tell you where you're going to go when you die, after life; what happens in the afterlife it will tell you. Now the second reason is to tell you morality, right or wrong. How do you know this is morally right? Killing is wrong for example, stealing is wrong, giving charity is good. So you need Revelation from God to know these things. Without Revelation you [cannot] know. So God sends you Revelation for that reason.", "So if you believe in the message of the prophets, and you believe that God sent these people because they come with evidences and people follow them, like Prophet Muhammad, is two billion people that follow him; Jesus, two billion people that follow him, in fact four billion because Muslims also believe in Jesus. So if you've got all of these billions of people believing in them, people when they were walking, they saw them performing acts that shows they from God, Miracles, and because of that people believed in them. Not only believed in them, they died for them, and when they died they carried on their message, like the prophet companion [carried] their message, Jesus companions [carried] their message, because they're messengers of God and they showed with evidences that they are from God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises A French Man Looking For Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piz443ivKUc", ((78, "1:18–1:43"), (108, "1:48–2:32"), 