#passage(("If there is a Creator, then would make perfect sense for him to send Messengers to tell us our purpose, because we didn't create ourself and you cannot come yourself to the conclusion of why do you exist. Many people say what's my purpose in life, but that is not an answer you can give. You can have a subjective purpose, doing something on the side, but what is the objective purpose of the existence of all Humanity? Only the one who made you can tell you. The one who made your watch, for example, is the one who is going to tell you the time. So that purpose of telling the time was given by the maker and the manufacturer. So the one who ascribes purpose to things is the one who designs and makes these things and objects. So those prophets and [messengers] come and tell us purpose.", "Muslims believe the purpose in this life, in this existence, is to be tested. This life is a test, and that test is whether you will do good and fulfill Yourself by connecting with the Creator, doing goodness in community and Society, or you will follow Satan and your own desires. There's only two ways, there's only two paths.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Students Ask Curious Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XLWOnl9JFok", ((230, "3:50–4:29"), (269, "4:29–4:46"),), id: 424)
