#passage(("If life is a test, then by default, there will be people who disobey God. Prophet Muhammad was sent because there's a difference now. It's not about obeying or disobeying God, but the idea that The Message itself has been corrupted by some people, changed. So God has to send a Messenger so he can tell people The Truth again. Then the test can be fair. So now, they know The Truth and they know what's false, and they can choose to either follow it or disobey.", "And Muslims are not perfect people. And I always say that starting by myself, we're not perfect. We believe everyone commits sins. Prophet Muhammad said that \"every child of Adam commits sins\". God doesn't ask you for perfection. In Islam, God just asks you, commands you to do your best. And if you sin, you repent, you come back, you return, etc. You rectify yourself. You stand up again after you fall. That's what life is about. Test is not about being perfect. If God wanted you to be perfect, He would have made you perfect. He made the angels who don't disobey God at all. He would have created us like them or more angels.", "So yes, there are Muslims who disobey, who do bad. Some of them are just normal Muslims because everyone sins. And some of them are doing big sins. So they're failing the test. But if it's a test, then there has to be people who will fail and there has to be people who will succeed. Otherwise, it's not really a test.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Baha'i Lady Questions Muslim On The Last Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_h1_yrAXLg", ((440, "7:20–7:43"), (492, "8:12–8:57"), (541, "9:01–9:18"),), id: 425)
