#passage(("In order for me and you to know about God, we need to have a Messenger to tell us about God. Because if you said I know about God by myself, everyone will make up his own idea of God. So, Allah chose His Messengers. So, Prophet Muhammadﷺ, we say, is the last Messenger in a line of different Messengers. So, I cannot just say I believe in Jesus, but I don't believe in Moses. I cannot say I believe in Prophet Muhammadﷺ but I reject other Messengers. I have to believe in all of them (Albaqara2:136). And that's the thing about Islam. It makes sense. It's rational. We cannot punish an innocent person for our sins.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Priests Force Their Beliefs?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SU-3La7AfR4", ((386, "6:26–7:01"),), id: 426)
