#passage(("Now about Messengers and Prophets of God. Allah says in the Quran (21:7) that if We were to send them down an angel, they will not relate to that angel. For example, Allah says 'Pray!' and the angel shows them how to pray; they will say 'That's a perfect being! I cannot imitate it, I cannot pray! Prayer is hard for me, You sent down a perfect being! If You send down a normal human being then maybe I can follow.'", "But if God sends a human being, and the human being demonstrates the best, perfect manners that human being can do, then you and me can learn from that as an example. And no one can come with excuses and say 'I can't do it'. A human being was before you and he did it, he's a human. So those are messengers that are people who demonstrate to us how to behave, how to relate, how to connect to the Creator. So that's why we believe in Messengers of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Student Challenges Muslim On Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0eOxOwACYXE", ((174, "2:54–3:33"), (217, "3:37–3:56"),), id: 427)
