#passage(("When it comes to Allahﷻ \"coming to us\": if there's someone in my house and I say come here and he comes, and I say go there and he goes, who has more authority, me or him? Me. So who is the Master and who's the servant in this relationship? When I say go over there, come here, I want you to come at 3:00 when I'm sleeping, come to me.", "So if we tell Allah to come, and Allah has to come to every single one of us when we want him to come to us, then it does not make any sense to say that Allah is the Creator, and He's the King and He's the Master and we're the servants. You flipped the relationship now. It became that we are the one demanding God to do what we want Him to do. Show me this sign the way I want, or you're not there. I'm now dictating to God what to do. So I'm the God in this relationship. He's not God because He's listening to my commands.", "We are created by Allahﷻ; this life is a test. If Allah comes to everyone in a dream and shows him an undoubtable Miracle of His existence that he can observe empirically, then there's no point in this life being a test for people. Allah is saying (those who believe in the Unseen) in the beginning of the Quran chapter:2 (Albaqarah2:2-3). How can you believe in the Unseen when you've already seen it?", "This question of yours is already answered in the Quran. Allah says: (If We willed, We could send down to them from the sky a sign for which their necks would remain humbled) (Ash-Shu'ara 26:4). That means they believe or they will be punished, because they've already seen evidence now. That's why when you look at the previous civilizations, when they've had all of these big miracles that Allah has shown through the Prophets, when they didn't believe they were punished. Because now that's it, you've seen the evidence now. You've seen a big, empirical miracle. We're talking about empirical ones; you can see with your own eyes things happening which are supernatural, and you still disbelieve, therefore you require punishment.", "So this life is a test, and people are being tested, therefore it would not make any sense for Allahﷻ to come to every single individual. Then why would Allah put you in this life to begin with? He could've just created you in the Sama سماء (the Sky) and you can see him, and that's it.", "And The Prophets and Messengers are communicating with Allahﷻ. Allah gives them Revelation; that is the reason they communicate with Allahﷻ directly. It's because they're used as agents to give the Revelation, the guidance to us, and the test is whether we will follow their Guidance, the Revelation that they brought, or we will choose our own desires and what we want to do and how we want to do it.", "If Allahﷻ were to appear to every single individual, that'd be the most confusing anarchy I've seen in my life. Imagine Allah comes to me and says for example that I'm the next Messenger, and then Allah comes to you and says that I'm not the next Messenger. Who should we trust? Every person comes and says: Allah said to me give me the keys to your house, and another person comes and says: No, Allah said actually do not give him the keys to your house. This is going to become ridiculous, to say that every single individual is going to have communication with Allah and he's going to bring information from his own mind of his experience with the Divine.", "Those Prophets and Messengers are selected for a reason, and that reason is because they are the best of their communities, and their job is just to deliver the Revelation; then people take the Revelation, follow it, or they choose their desires and Satan. There's no other way. Allah says: \"فَإِن لَّمْ يَسْتَجِيبُوا لَكَ\" (If they do not respond to your Message) \"فَاعْلَمْ أَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُونَ أَهْوَاءَهُمْ\" (then know that they only follow their desires) \"وَمَنْ أَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ اتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ بِغَيْرِ هُدًى مِّنَ اللَّهِ\" (Al-Qasas 28:50) (and who is more misguided than one who follows his desire without guidance from Allah?) There is no one more misguided than this, those people who believe they are apes. This is the level of misguidance you would reach without Revelation, without guidance coming from Allahﷻ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Afghan Girl Claims That Muslims Are Blind Followers?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7HhWSHopwFc", ((1717, "28:37–28:56"), (1742, "29:02–29:25"), (1765, "29:25–29:46"), (1788, "29:48–30:18"), (1820, "30:20–30:30"), (1836, "30:36–30:50"), (1856, "30:56–31:26"), (1890, "31:30–31:59"),), id: 430)
