#passage(("\"Why does God not communicate to us?\" In basic terms Allahﷻ responses to that in The Quran2:118: وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِینَ لَا یَعۡلَمُونَ لَوۡلَا یُكَلِّمُنَا ٱللَّهُ أَوۡ تَأۡتِینَاۤ ءَایَةࣱۗ Allah says they say (why would God not speak to us?) or (a sign comes to us?) and Allah says (this is how the people before them disbelieved) and then Allah says (Allah has made the signs clear). Allah does not need to talk to you because He's given you enough signs to know that Allah exists. He's given you enough signs around you to know that this book is from God. He sent you multiple Prophets and Messengers to know that this is the Revelation coming from The Creator. Now, we don't say the Disciples were speaking to Allah directly; we say only The Prophets and Messengers were getting Revelation from God. The Disciples were the followers of The Prophets and Messengers. This is a definition of A Prophet: someone who receives the [revelation] from God.", "Now the point is this; if I'm a King and I send you a Messenger, and that Messenger has a Message and the Message says David leave the car, and the Messenger comes and he gives you the Message. And then you take the Message, the letter, and you put it on your desk. Let's say now five years later and I want you to leave the car and you have the letter still on your desk. Do I need to send you another Messenger saying you the same thing, or it's enough because you already have the Message?", "The Message is here, which is The Quran, which is completely preserved from the time of Prophet Muhammad peace be upon him, with perfect Guidance that is not time bound. The Guidance in The Quran is for all time. So if the Message is there, perfect, preserved, the Guidance is there, is enough for us until the Day of Judgment, why does God need to send another Messenger saying to you the same thing? Allah has showed you (Quran2:118) قَدْ بَيَّنَّا الْآيَاتِ ِAyat are clear, the verses, the signs are clear for people who use reasoning and intellect.", "We do need God more than before! God is still there! How many people are religious in the world? There are more religious people than non-religious people. Just because someone is not following God, does not mean God is out of the picture. Muslims; two billion people in the world are believing in God, worshipping God on a daily basis. If you count Christians, though they aren't practising, there are another two billion. If you count the Jews, if you count the Hindus, all of these people are still connected to a higher power, or they're saying there is a higher power. God is always in the picture and will always be. The question is are you following or you are not following?", "This movement of Atheism is a new thing of people who have problems with science because The Bible was anti-scientific and the Church was anti-Science and they were killing the scientists and burning them alive and this and that, so this new movement of Atheism came. But we didn't have this issue ever in the peak of Islamic Civilisation; science was a basic part of human practices in the Muslim Civilisation.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Does God Not Communicate With Humans? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1c92faSXNec", ((904, "15:04–15:46"), (951, "15:51–16:06"), (975, "16:15–16:40"), (1020, "17:00–17:32"), (1057, "17:37–17:50"),), id: 431)
