#passage(("From our perspective, we have an answer for that question, and we don't think what you're saying is logical. You're saying that people created religions to comfort themselves and answer the questions that they don't have an answer for. We, as Muslims, have a very unique position that deals with this issue. The word Muslim means someone who submits his will to the One True Creator. Anyone who submits to the One True God, the Creator of the Universe, the real God, not fake idols or fake deities, that person is called a Muslim. Because the word Muslim comes from the word اسْتِسْلام which is Submission, and a Muslim is someone who does the act of submission. So he's called a Submitter, a Muslim. That's the literal translation of the word. What we say as Muslims is that the first human being that God created, God: Allah, has given him guidance, has given him directions, has given him answers.", "God creates. God says \"Be!\" and it is, and He creates. That's our belief about the Creator. Our definition of God, literally, is an Entity which is All-Powerful. An entity which is All-Powerful can create by just saying \"Be!\" and it is. This is the answer to \"how?\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is Atheism Rational? Atheist Challenges Muslim! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFzWhMCQFn4", ((1705, "28:25–29:42"), (1795, "29:55–30:22"),), id: 434)
