#passage(("That's not the only reason why religion is good. I'll tell you why it's incorrect. It's incorrect from every aspect. First, from the aspect of a personal experience, what benefits you as a human being in believing in a religion? Now if we compare it to Western philosophy: just doubt everything, doubt your existence, you have no conclusions, you have no premises. That is the personal thing; there's no benefit essentially. Talk about following religion, there are tons of benefits, whether it is your relationship with God which gives you spiritual fortitude and strength, mental strength. It also gives you answers for the suffering that you go through in life. Gives you community and purpose as a human being. Gives you guidance in life. What is the good things that you need to do? What is the bad things that you need to avoid? You get nothing from Western philosophy.", "If I were to take you right now and put you in my basement and start taking your nails off one by one and wait for them to grow and keep repeating the process, you will care about suffering. Why? Because it's happening to you. Right now you're saying that is because you live an easy life. There are tons of people who are in active suffering and they would care about suffering and explanations for it, and they would need mental fortitude for it. Why do people commit suicide? Because many people come to that conclusion of absolute suffering in which there's no purpose, nihilism.", "On a personal level it gives you answers to these questions, cuz there's many people who don't have families. Then what are you going to live for? So it's not just about a family religion; it's about your connection with God, your purpose in this life and where are you going in the afterlife? But you will die one day, and if there is a God, your fulfillment is irrelevant because there will be a punishment for not following the command.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist And Muslim Debate Western Philosophy! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-8wK8kZGyY", ((872, "14:32–15:39"), (953, "15:53–16:23"), (1013, "16:53–17:20"),), id: 435)

